.Dd October 2, 2026
.Dt TUNE2FS 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm tune2fs ,
.Nm e2label
.Nd change and list the settings of an ext2 file system
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl fl
.Op Fl c Ar max-mount-counts
.Op Fl C Ar mount-count
.Op Fl e Ar errors-behavior
.Op Fl E Ar extended-options
.Op Fl g Ar group
.Op Fl i Ar interval Ns Op Cm d Ns | Ns Cm m Ns | Ns Cm w
.Op Fl L Ar volume-label
.Op Fl m Ar reserved-percentage
.Op Fl M Ar last-mounted-directory
.Op Fl o Oo ^ Oc Ns Ar mount-option Ns Op , Ns Ar ...
.Op Fl O Oo ^ Oc Ns Ar feature Ns Op , Ns Ar ...
.Op Fl r Ar reserved-blocks
.Op Fl T Ar time-last-checked
.Op Fl u Ar user
.Op Fl U Ar UUID
.Op Fl z Ar undo-file
.Ar device
.Nm e2label
.Ar device
.Op Ar volume-label
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
changes the settings an ext2 volume keeps in its superblock, and with
.Fl l
lists them.
.Ar device
is a partition node, a loop device or a file that holds a volume.
.Nm e2label
is the same program by another name: it prints the volume's label, or
sets it to
.Ar volume-label .
.Pp
Rach2 uses e2fsprogs 1.47.4, linked statically against the ported musl,
and installs it on the GNU system at
.Pa /sbin/tune2fs ,
with
.Pa /sbin/e2label
a link to it.
The ordinary kernel takes no write to a disk node, so there
.Nm
lists a partition's settings and changes those of a volume in a file or on
a loop device; a change of a partition answers
.Er EPERM .
.Nm
reads
.Pa /proc/mounts
to find whether the volume is mounted.
.Pp
The kernel mounts read-only a volume with
.Ql dir_index
or a read-only-compatible feature it does not know, and refuses one with
an incompatible feature other than
.Ql filetype ;
see
.Xr mke2fs 8 .
So
.Fl O Cm dir_index
leaves a volume the kernel mounts read-only, and
.Fl j
or
.Fl O Cm extent
one it does not mount writable.
The kernel keeps no mount count and no time of the last check, so
.Fl c ,
.Fl C ,
.Fl i
and
.Fl T
set fields only
.Xr e2fsck 8
reads.
.Pp
The options are upstream's:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl c Ar max-mount-counts
The number of mounts after which
.Ql e2fsck -p
checks the volume; 0 or -1 for none.
.It Fl C Ar mount-count
The number of mounts so far.
.It Fl e Ar errors-behavior
What a kernel does on finding an error:
.Cm continue ,
.Cm remount-ro
or
.Cm panic ;
this kernel does not read it.
.It Fl E Ar extended-options
Upstream's extended options, comma-separated, such as
.Cm stride= Ns Ar n
and
.Cm mount_opts= Ns Ar string .
.It Fl f
Force a change upstream would otherwise refuse.
.It Fl g Ar group
The group that may use the reserved blocks.
.It Fl i Ar interval
The longest time between checks, in days, or in months or weeks with
.Cm m
or
.Cm w ;
0 for none.
.It Fl l
List the superblock's settings, as
.Ql dumpe2fs -h
does.
.It Fl L Ar volume-label
The label, up to 16 bytes.
.It Fl m Ar reserved-percentage
The share of blocks kept for the user and group of
.Fl u
and
.Fl g .
.It Fl M Ar last-mounted-directory
The directory recorded as the last mount point.
.It Fl o Ar mount-options
Default mount options, each removed with a leading
.Ql ^ ;
the kernel reads none of them.
.It Fl O Ar features
Features to set, each removed with a leading
.Ql ^ .
.It Fl r Ar reserved-blocks
The number of reserved blocks.
.It Fl T Ar time-last-checked
The time of the last check, as
.Ar YYYYMMDD Ns Op Ar HH Ns Op Ar MM Ns Op Ar SS ,
or
.Cm now .
.It Fl u Ar user
The user that may use the reserved blocks.
.It Fl U Ar UUID
A new UUID:
.Cm clear ,
.Cm random ,
.Cm time
or a UUID.
.It Fl z Ar undo-file
Save the blocks the change overwrites in
.Ar undo-file
first.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /sbin/tune2fs
.It Pa /sbin/tune2fs
The program on the GNU system.
.It Pa /sbin/e2label
A link to it.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Nm
exits 0 on success and 1 on an error.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Label a volume in a file and read the label back:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# tune2fs -L data /root/vol.ext2
# e2label /root/vol.ext2
data
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr loop 4 ,
.Xr dumpe2fs 8 ,
.Xr e2fsck 8 ,
.Xr mke2fs 8
